// Ch9 B01/B02: talking to Toma on the strand (docs/kb/story/beats/act1_ch09.md B01 "Kerrid is nowhere",
// §4 the side scene). One talk prompt on Toma, who has gone to kneel at one shroud in the Stillguard row:
// while the side scene is open (ch08_met_ivo, Ch8 B02, always set on the critical path; not yet played)
// it plays "Shield-Mate"; otherwise Rhen asks after Kerrid, and nobody looks for him. The chapter flow
// offers the prompt only before the Ebbing (B03), as the sheet asks.
title: ch09_toma
location: ch09/corrow_night
---
<<if $ch08_met_ivo and not $ch09_toma_knelt_with_ivo>>
    <<jump ch09_shield_mate>>
<<endif>>
Rhen [neutral]: Seen Kerrid? #line:ch09_toma_001
Toma [neutral]: Not since the stair. #line:ch09_toma_002
===
// B02, the optional side scene "Shield-Mate" (§4; E, ~4 min, ~170 words). N05: the row where the Corrow
// garrison has laid out its own dead with their round shields at their feet, one locked 50 mm shot plus
// two inserts (N05A, the end of Toma's indigo sash wiping the salt; N05B, Ivo's face, peaceful, washed by
// the sea, the broken tooth showing a little: the ONLY uncovered dead face in Ch9, never wounded).
// Toma is kneeling at Ivo Brannick's shroud with the cloth folded back. Rhen comes and stands near;
// Toma doesn't look up; Rhen doesn't joke. Nothing about the 1003 burning is said beyond "the same line,
// at the shoals" (do not surface). Toma keeps "Be level" (his faith is intact in Act I). No more than four
// Toma lines in a row. Asha passes on her way to the raft at the end (staging note: the sheet has the
// gilt line fresh on her face here, but B03 is its first appearance; flagged for Narrative's review).
// Toma is asking for his friend to be led into the sea: love, wrong in hindsight, played with no wink.
title: ch09_shield_mate
---
@letterbox on
@camera N05
@music silence fade=1.5
@sfx harbour_lap
@wait 2.0
@mark rhen ivo_stand walk
@wait 2.0
@camera N05A
@anim toma wipe_face
@wait 1.5
Toma [grief]: He could not tie a hook knot. Seven years on this wall. I tied all of his. #line:ch09_shield_001
@camera N05
Rhen [sad]: You served with him long? #line:ch09_shield_002
Toma [sad]: Seven years. We stood on the same line once. At the shoals. #line:ch09_shield_003
Rhen [neutral]: Where we found Liss? #line:ch09_shield_004
@wait 2.5
Toma [neutral]: Another camp. Another year. #line:ch09_shield_005
@wait 2.0
@camera N05B
@wait 1.5
@anim toma fold_cloth
@camera N05
@wait 1.0
Toma [tender]: Be level. #line:ch09_shield_006 #tn:"The Stillguard's greeting. A living comrade answers 'And still.' The dead man can't."
@wait 3.0
-> And still. #line:ch09_shield_007
    <<set $ch09_rhen_answered_toma = true>>
    @face toma grief 1.0
    Toma [grief]: Thank you. #line:ch09_shield_008
-> (Say nothing.) #line:ch09_shield_009
    @wait 2.0
    Toma [grief]: And still. #line:ch09_shield_010 #tn:"Said very quietly, answering for the dead man himself."
<<set $ch09_toma_knelt_with_ivo = true>>
@mark asha asha_passing walk
@wait 2.5
@anim toma look_at asha
Toma [tender]: Asha. Take him gently. #line:ch09_shield_011
Asha [tender]: I'll take him first. #line:ch09_shield_012
@wait 1.5
@letterbox off
@camera release
===
